  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RWI: HR education and capacity development, 2013-2019</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">RWI: MR utbildning och kapacitetsutveckling, 2013-2019</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RWI&apos;s Cambodia Human Rights Capacity Development Programme has been supported by the Embassy since 2012. The intervention aims to strengthen environment for human rights promotion and protection in Cambodia. In order to achieve this goal, RWI has established an office in Cambodia and forged collaboration with a number of key relevant institutions that have the capacity and mandate to make a positive impact on human rights situation in Cambodia on the academic, policy and implementation level. RWI works with institutions that train and educate the next generation of decision-makers in Cambodia. RWI supports the development of a neutral academic platform which can contribute to better informed debates, increased cooperation and coordination between government institutions and civil society organisations and provide inputs to policy development. RWI also contributes to providing inputs into the bilateral human rights dialogue between Sweden and Cambodia.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">RWI:s kapacitetsutvecklingsprogram inom m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter i Kambodja har st&#xf6;tts av ambassaden sedan 2012 och avslutas 31 december 2019. Insatsen syftar till att st&#xe4;rka m&#xf6;jligheterna att verka f&#xf6;r och skydda de m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheterna i Kambodja. F&#xf6;r att uppn&#xe5; planerade resultat har RWI etablerat ett kontor i Kambodja och inlett samarbete med ett antal relevanta nyckelinstitutioner som har kapacitet och mandat att positivt p&#xe5;verka MR-situationen i landet p&#xe5; akademisk, policy och implementerande niv&#xe5;. RWI arbetar med institutioner som utbildar n&#xe4;sta generations beslutsfattare i Kambodja. RWI st&#xf6;djer utvecklandet av en neutral akademisk plattform som avser bidra till mer informerade debatter, &#xf6;kat samarbete och samordning mellan myndigheter och civilsamh&#xe4;lle samt bidra till policyutveckling. RWI bidrar vidare med underlag till den bilaterala MR-dialogen mellan Kambodja och Sverige.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the Programme was to &#x201c;strengthen the environment for human rights promotion and protection in Cambodia&#x201d; through strengthening the institutional capacities of selected academic institutions to develop and deliver high-quality human rights education and research as well as providing an academic platform for human rights debates and dialogue, and for strategically selected government institutions to fulfil their obligations in accordance with international human rights standards. Furthermore, the programme aimed to contribute to the effective conduct of the bilateral dialogue on Human Rights between Cambodia and Sweden.</narrative>
  </description>
